sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: The table list — load once, reuse, and refresh
    accDescr: The browser and server save table lists to avoid repeated discovery. This sequence shows loading when saved information is needed, followed by explicit refresh. Database discovery is skipped when the server already has a saved copy. Refresh replaces saved copies only on success and does not update other tabs or servers.
    autonumber
    participant B as Browser
    participant APP as App server
    participant DB as Database

    B->>APP: Load the table and column list
    APP->>DB: Read the list if no server copy is saved
    DB-->>APP: Accessible tables and columns
    APP-->>B: Save and show the list
    Note over B,APP: Normal browsing reuses saved copies.

    B->>APP: User clicks Refresh
    APP->>DB: Request current tables and columns
    DB-->>APP: Updated table list
    APP-->>B: Replace saved copies after success
    Note over B,DB: If refresh fails, keep the last good list. Other tabs and servers refresh separately.
